<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/12th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Ourique</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1139</span> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reconquista">Reconquista</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Ourique was fought in 1139 in the south of present-day Portugal, where <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afonso-i-of-portugal">Afonso Henriques</a> defeated Muslim forces. The victory became the traditional founding moment of the independent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-portugal">Kingdom of Portugal</a>. The site lists it among the reverses on the northern Iberian front that weakened the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravid Empire</a> during its decline.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-ourique.jpg" alt="Battle of Ourique" width="320" height="161" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Domingos Sequeira · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:BatalhaOurique.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
